================================================================================
PHASE 1 — ORIENT (Gap Analysis & Strategic Decisions)
================================================================================

## GAP 1.1 Design System Compliance
**Observation**: No automated verification that components use correct Tailwind tokens
**Risk**: Design drift, inconsistent styling, hardcoded values creeping in
**Decision**: ACT — Visual regression tests for critical components

## GAP 1.2 RWD Verification
**Observation**: No automated testing of responsive breakpoints
**Risk**: Layout breaks, overflow, hidden content at certain viewports
**Decision**: ACT — Playwright viewport matrix tests

## GAP 1.3 Carousel Functionality
**Observation**: Single drawer carousel test exists, but no product carousel tests
**Risk**: Navigation bugs, slide visibility issues, animation failures
**Decision**: ACT — Comprehensive carousel interaction tests

## GAP 1.4 Accessibility
**Observation**: No automated a11y checks (axe-core, role verification)
**Risk**: WCAG violations, screen reader incompatibility
**Decision**: ACT — Integrate @axe-core/playwright

## GAP 1.5 Performance (CLS, LCP)
**Observation**: No automated Core Web Vitals verification
**Risk**: Layout shifts, slow LCP affecting SEO/UX
**Decision**: DEFER — Separate performance test sprint

## GAP 1.6 Component Isolation
**Observation**: No Storybook or component isolation environment
**Risk**: Components tested only in full page context, hard to debug
**Decision**: DEFER — Storybook setup requires separate sprint

================================================================================
PHASE 2 — DECIDE (Test Strategy Architecture)
================================================================================

TESTING PYRAMID FOR HOMEPAGE:

```
       /\
      /  \        E2E Flows (5%)
     /    \       Critical user paths
    /______\
   /        \     Integration (15%)
  /          \    Carousel + Grid behavior
 /____________\
/              \  Component (30%)
/                \ Section rendering, cards
/__________________\
                    Unit (50%)
                    Utilities, helpers, data
```

SEQUENCE RATIONALE:
1. **Foundation**: Unit tests for utilities (fast feedback, cheap)
2. **Structure**: Component tests for sections (isolated verification)
3. **Integration**: Carousel/Grid behavior (component interaction)
4. **E2E**: Full page flows (cross-browser, viewport matrix)
5. **Visual**: Design system compliance (regression prevention)

