CI/CD INTEGRATION
================================================================================

**GitHub Actions** (update existing):
```yaml
# .github/workflows/playwright.yml
- name: Run Homepage Tests
  run: npx playwright test tests/e2e/homepage/
  env:
    PLAYWRIGHT_PROJECT: chromium  # Fast feedback
    
- name: Run RWD Matrix
  run: npx playwright test tests/e2e/homepage/rwd-matrix.spec.ts
  if: github.event_name == 'pull_request'
```

**Test Scripts** (add to package.json):
```json
{
  "test:homepage:unit": "vitest run tests/unit/homepage/",
  "test:homepage:component": "npx playwright test-ct tests/component/",
  "test:homepage:e2e": "npx playwright test tests/e2e/homepage/",
  "test:homepage:regression": "npx playwright test tests/e2e/homepage/regression.spec.ts",
  "test:homepage:a11y": "npx playwright test tests/e2e/homepage/accessibility.spec.ts"
}
```

================================================================================
ARCHITECTURE DECISIONS (Record)
================================================================================

1. **Test Runner Selection**: 
   - Vitest for unit (speed, Vite integration)
   - Playwright for component/E2E (real browser, RWD testing)
   - Rationale: JSDOM misses layout/styling bugs

2. **Component Testing Strategy**:
   - Playwright CT over Storybook (for now)
   - Rationale: Faster setup, no additional infrastructure
   - Future: Storybook for design system documentation

3. **Mock Strategy**:
   - Mock all API calls in component tests
   - Use test database or mocks in E2E
   - Rationale: Deterministic tests, no external dependencies

4. **Viewport Matrix**:
   - 6 viewports covering 95% of traffic
   - Not testing every possible size (impractical)
   - Rationale: Balance coverage vs. execution time

5. **Accessibility Approach**:
   - Automated: axe-core for WCAG violations
   - Manual: Keyboard navigation tests
   - Rationale: Automated catches 80%, manual catches rest

================================================================================
RISKS & MITIGATION
================================================================================

| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |
|------|-----------|--------|------------|
| Flaky carousel tests | Medium | High | Add retry logic, wait for animations |
| Slow E2E execution | Medium | Medium | Parallel execution, shard tests |
| Test data maintenance | Medium | Medium | Centralized fixtures, version control |
| Visual flakiness | Low | Medium | Screenshot thresholds, masked regions |
| Axe-core false positives | Low | Low | Manual review process for new violations |

